On 11/9/06, Matt Arnold <matt.mattarn@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Hugh, there's no cause here to worked up into a hysteria.


Wow, hysteria?  I didn't mean to give that impression.  I thought two short
paragraphs was reasonable.  My mental state while writing that was actually
one of relief!

Anyone who doesn't like Lojban is free to make a new language.


Agreed.  And since Bob's the one who disregards the value of the CLL, and
actively obstructs explorations and valid queries on the extent of Lojban
that he personally doesn't like, _his_ is the 'new' language.  Hey Bob, Matt
says you're free to make a new language!  So do I, actually.  (Though I
would advise you carefully label it a 'variant' of Lojban.  You know how
pedants are.)

Lojbab has been correct on every
> point he's made in this thread.


That's as may be, but the last point remains: Bob is not here for the
benefit of this community (he will actively and happily cause strife to
serve his purposes), and he's not here for the benefit of the Lojban
language (except the particular version that lives inside his own skull).

mi'e .xius.
--
Good night, and have a rational tomorrow!

